---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Install — Hornero OS"
  description="How to install Hornero OS: profiles, requirements, status."
>
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>
      HorneroOS is pre-release. The composition model is defined — release
      manifests pin every component — and three profiles exist: 
      <code class="inline">base</code>, <code class="inline">desktop</code>, and 
      <code class="inline">developer</code>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Start with the 
        <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/docs">documentation</a> and the 
        <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/hornero">composition repo</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        On Arch today: install <code class="inline">horneroctl</code> from AUR
        and drive the desktop from one CLI.
      </li>
      <li>
        The guided installer (archinstall, Calamares, or custom — undecided) is
        bound by the 
        <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/installer">staged install contract</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Requirements: Arch Linux, Hyprland, Quickshell. The greeter needs SDDM
      plus Qt6 Multimedia.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
